        "findings": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe overall shape is right: this is exactly where the family of derived-field methods lives (`displayName`, `membershipNumber`, `locality`, `contactPreference`, `identityKey`, \u2026), each with a matching `@Mapping(... expression = \"java(x(owner))\")` and a documented `default` method with null guards. `ageBand` slots into that pattern cleanly \u2014 right unit, no duplication, no catch-all growth, and the schema/model/SQL additions are all consistent and additive. One idiomatic nit worth fixing:\n\n- **Inline fully-qualified type names in `ageBand` break the file's convention.** The method body uses `java.time.LocalDate` (twice) and `java.time.Period` fully qualified inline, whereas every other method in this interface refers to its types by simple name via imports at the top (e.g. `OwnerDto.ContactPreferenceEnum` in `contactPreference`). These are ordinary default-method bodies (not MapStruct `expression=` strings, which is the only place FQNs would be forced), so add `import java.time.LocalDate;` and `import java.time.Period;` and use `LocalDate` / `Period` in the body to match the surrounding style. As written it reads as a foreign insertion rather than a natural part of the file."
